log-archive /var/log -s "0 2 * * *"       # every day at 02:00
log-archive /var/log -s "0 0 * * 0"       # every Sunday at midnight
log-archive /var/log -s "0 */6 * * *"     # every 6 hours
log-archive /var/log --remove-cron        # uninstall the job
```

---

### What gets produced

| Output | Description |
|---|---|
| `logs_archive_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.tar.gz` | Timestamped compressed archive |
| `archive_activity.log` | Appended log of every run — date, source, file count, raw size, compressed size, ratio |

The activity log looks like:
```
[2024-08-16 10:06:48]  archive=logs_archive_20240816_100648.tar.gz  source=/var/log  files=42  raw=18.23 MB  compressed=2.41 MB  ratio=86.8%
